    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **Tests run: 62, Failures: 0, Errors: 0** \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, including the new `Cp50Tests.coreIdempotentRepeat`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented idempotent owner creation in `OwnerRestControllerV1` (the `POST /api/owners` handler).\n\nSince the OpenAPI-generated `OwnersApi` interface fixes the `addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` signature, I read the header out-of-band via an injected `HttpServletRequest` rather than altering the generated contract.\n\nChanges in `src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\n- Injected `HttpServletRequest` (constructor) to read the `Idempotency-Key` header.\n- Added an `idempotentCreates` `ConcurrentHashMap<String, OwnerDto>` that records the owner originally created under each seen key.\n- In `addOwner`, before any validation/creation: if the request carries an `Idempotency-Key` already present in the store, return the originally created owner with **200 OK** \u2014 no duplicate, no re-running the create rules.\n- After a successful create, cache the resulting `OwnerDto` under the key; the first create still returns **201 Created** as before.\n\nBehavior when no key (or a blank key) is present is unchanged, so all existing checkpoint tests remain green.\n\nA note on scope: the store is an in-process map (fine for these tests and a single instance). If you later want durability or multi-instance correctness, that key\u2192owner mapping would need to move to shared/persistent storage \u2014 happy to do that if it's a requirement.",
