    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered sequence for `addOwner` (POST /api/owners), traced from `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` at lines 824\u2013888. Everything below happens in this exact order.\n\n## Before the method body\n\n1. **Authorization** (`@PreAuthorize`, line 822) \u2014 caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role, else 403.\n2. **Bean Validation on the request body** \u2014 the DTO's constraints reject `null`/empty required fields (per the comments at lines 147\u2013153, this catches nulls and empty strings but *not* whitespace-only values).\n\n## Inside the method\n\n3. **Idempotency replay check** (lines 825\u2013831) \u2014 reads the `Idempotency-Key` header; if non-blank and already seen, returns the previously stored owner with **200 OK** and does nothing further (short-circuit).\n\n4. **Address composition & normalization** (lines 832\u2013845) \u2014 if `addressLine1` is non-blank, normalize line 1 (and line 2 if present) and compose them; otherwise normalize the single `address` field. Normalization = trim, collapse internal whitespace, upper-case, and expand street abbreviations (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`).\n\n5. **Required/blank-field guard** (line 846, `rejectMissingOrBlankFields`) \u2014 rejects with **400** (`MissingOwnerFieldsException`, listing offending fields) if any of `firstName`, `lastName`, composed `address`, `city`, `telephone` is null or whitespace-only.\n\n6. **City capacity check** (line 847, `rejectCityAtCapacity`) \u2014 rejects with **409** (`CityAtCapacityException`) if the city (case-insensitive) already holds \u2265 50 owners.\n\n7. **Map DTO \u2192 Owner entity** (line 849) and set the normalized address / line1 / line2 (lines 850\u2013852).\n\n8. **Telephone normalization** (lines 853\u2013854, `normalizeTelephone`) \u2014 strips spaces/dashes/brackets, applies `+61` default (dropping a leading `0`), requires valid E.164 (`+` then 8\u201315 digits), and enforces per-country national length (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210). Invalid \u2192 **400** (`InvalidTelephoneException`). Result stored on the owner.\n\n9. **Email normalization** (lines 855\u2013856, `normalizeEmail`) \u2014 `null` is allowed; otherwise must match the email pattern and its domain must not be on the disposable-domain block list; valid value is lower-cased. Invalid/disposable \u2192 **400** (`InvalidEmailException`). Result stored on the owner.\n\n10. **Postcode validation** (line 857, `validatePostcode`) \u2014 `null` allowed; else must be exactly 4 digits, and if the city maps to a known region the postcode must fall in that region's range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099). Invalid \u2192 **400** (`InvalidPostcodeException`).\n\n11. **Compute householdId** (line 858) \u2014 derived from collapsed `lastName` + `postcode` (used next and stored later).\n\n12. **Hard duplicate-identity check** (line 859, `rejectDuplicateIdentity`) \u2014 scans all non-deleted owners and rejects with **409** on: matching normalized telephone (`DuplicateTelephoneException`), matching lower-cased email (`DuplicateEmailException`), or matching `householdId` unless the caller set `sharesHousehold=true` (`DuplicateHouseholdException`).\n\n13. **Future registration-date check** (line 860, `rejectFutureRegistrationDate`) \u2014 a supplied `registrationDate` later than today \u2192 **400** (`FutureRegistrationDateException`); `null` allowed.\n\n14. **Effective date defaulting + business-day roll-forward** (lines 861\u2013862) \u2014 default a null date to today, then advance any Saturday/Sunday/listed public holiday to the next business day.\n\n15. **Daily owner-limit check** (line 863, `rejectDailyOwnerLimit`) \u2014 if \u2265 100 owners already carry that (rolled) registration date \u2192 **429** (`DailyOwnerLimitExceededException`).\n\n## Side-effects applied to the new owner (all before save)\n\n16. **Set `bulkSignupWarning`** (line 864) \u2014 true if > 80 owners already carry that